tations":[{"id":"1775506359551","neuronKeys":[],"edgeStrings":["[#4ac6f]_#_[#67239]","[#8e8fa]_#_[#67239]","[#8e8fa]_#_[#d310e]","[#caa4f]_#_[#d310e]","[#05551]_#_[#06f17]","[#9e4b7]_#_[#06f17]","[#05551]_#_[#9e98c]","[#e784d]_#_[#9e98c]"],"description":"This network produces an exploratory behavior, controlling the motors with various spontanious and triggered activations.","thumbnail":""},{"id":"1775506391172","neuronKeys":["[#91702]"],"edgeStrings":["[#91702]_#_[#e784d]","[#91702]_#_[#9e4b7]"],"description":"This neuron is occasionally active, and will send a spike at random every second or so.","thumbnail":""},{"id":"1775506471831","neuronKeys":["[#e784d]","[#9e4b7]"],"edgeStrings":["[#e784d]_#_[#9e98c]","[#9e4b7]_#_[#06f17]"],"description":"These neurons burst when they are activated, producing a stronger output suitable for driving motors. They will both activate, when stimulated from the random ocassionally active parent neuron.","thumbnail":""},{"id":"1775506579141","neuronKeys":["[#05551]"],"edgeStrings":["[#05551]_#_[#9e98c]","[#05551]_#_[#06f17]"],"description":"This neurongenerates longer bursts of activity, at random. It also triggers roughly once or so per second, but triggers for a longer length of time. You can drive the motors directly, or send signals to other neurons.","thumbnail":""},{"id":"1775506579177","neuronKeys":["[#05551]"],"edgeStrings":["[#05551]_#_[#9e98c]","[#05551]_#_[#06f17]"],"description":"This neurongenerates longer bursts of activity, at random. It also triggers roughly once or so per second, but triggers for a longer length of time. You can drive the motors directly, or send signals to other neurons.","thumbnail":""},{"id":"1775506631111","neuronKeys":["[#4ac6f]","[#caa4f]"],"edgeStrings":["[#4ac6f]_#_[#67239]","[#caa4f]_#_[#d310e]"],"description":"These two neurons also generate bursts just like the last one. But since these are different neurons, they will spike at different times, further guiding SpikerBot to explore and turn.","thumbnail":""},{"id":"1775506699773","neuronKeys":["[#8e8fa]"],"edgeStrings":["[#5ec60]_#_[#8e8fa]","[#8e8fa]_#_[#67239]","[#8e8fa]_#_[#d310e]","[#8e8fa]_#_[#16759]","[#8e8fa]_#_[#eac80]"],"description":"When SpikerBot gets stuck in a corner, this quiet neuron will activate. SpikerBot will blink red, say Uh-oh, and drive in reverse quickly to avoid the obstacle.","thumbnail":""},{"id":"1775506776124","neuronKeys":["[#4ac6f]","[#05551]","[#caa4f]","[#91702]","[#e784d]","[#9e4b7]"],"edgeStrings":["[#91702]_#_[#9e4b7]","[#91702]_#_[#e784d]","[#4ac6f]_#_[#67239]","[#caa4f]_#_[#d310e]","[#05551]_#_[#06f17]","[#e784d]_#_[#9e98c]","[#05551]_#_[#9e98c]","[#9e4b7]_#_[#06f17]"],"description":"How would you change these neurons and synapses to make SpikerBot explore differently?","thumbnail":""}],"info":{"title":"Explorer","description":"SpikerBot explores the world at random and tries to not get stuck!","author":"User","version":"1.0.1","timestamp":"2026-04-08T15:48:27.801933"}}